    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Kyle Tucker** anchoring the lineup, serving as the two highest-rated starters at 76.41 and 75.40, respectively. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Lowder (xERA 4.84), where his elite plate discipline and current form provide significant upside despite a slight platoon dip. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** is primed for a massive outing against Wilkinson; the combination of a positive wind shift and the opposing starter\u2019s mediocre skill set creates a perfect storm for extra-base production. **Miguel Vargas** (65.93), **Jackson Merrill** (65.51), **Andy Pages** (65.35), and **Henry Bolte** (65.23) round out our high-floor tier, with **Henry Bolte** specifically benefiting from a projected leadoff spot and favorable park factors that elevate his score well above his baseline.\n\nThe decision to keep **Wade Meckler** (40.28) on the bench was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Wade Meckler** provides valuable contact skills, the optimizer favored the defensive and situational utility of our middle infield options like **Nasim Nunez** (57.20), whose switch-hitting versatility and superior sprint speed profile offer more utility in our quest for stolen bases. Risks remain across the board, particularly with **Henry Bolte**, whose projected score assumes he hits at the top of the order; should his official lineup placement move down, his scoring efficiency will likely retract. We are also monitoring the heavy schedule load for **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin**, both of whom are hovering in the marginal 50s; they are active today, but their output will dictate if we need to lean harder into bench reserves like **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, or **Heliot Ramos** in future sets. With **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Curtis Mead** unavailable, we are managing depth carefully to preserve game caps while remaining aggressive in the stolen base category.",
